Z||000008||LZeitgeist||12-02-2001||06:14 PM||||Microsoft may have the money to be able to afford 'marketing muscle', but if people don't acually *like* the console and controllers and *buy* the games, it doesn't matter *how* much hype Microsoft generates for the X-Box... <P>If I had to choose one right this very second, I'd go for the PS2 because it already has the entire PlayStation support network and customer base as a solid foundation... X-Box, while nifty, is as yet unproven, and Microsoft software is rather infamous for its bugs... I'm sure it's nothing they won't work out, but I don't really want to be anybody's guinea pig.<P>Just my thoughts...||||reg||1
